# ==============================================================================
# GLOBAL ENVIRONMENT SAMPLE
# ==============================================================================
# The values shared by EVERY project. The gmake Makefile loads them before a
# project's own .env, which always wins.
#
# Build your copy and fill it in:
#   gmake env_global_enable
#
# That command reads this sample and every pack's, and writes
# ~/.config/zsh/gmake/.env.global — adding the variables that are missing,
# never rewriting one that is already there. Run it again after adding a pack.
#
# RULE: only values shared by ALL your projects belong here — geographic and
# technical defaults, machine-level settings. Anything that identifies a
# specific project goes in that project's .env (see .env.project.sample).
# ENFORCED: project-identifying variables are refused here at load time with
# an explicit error (see PROJECT_IDENTIFYING_VARS in the Makefile).
# ==============================================================================

# --- Optional default template for direct copier_project/cruft_project calls
# (fnew always picks from the catalog interactively) ---
# PROJECT_TEMPLATE_REPO=
# PROJECT_TEMPLATE_VERSION=

# The tools that need a default of their own bring it with them: their samples
# sit next to their modules, and `gmake env_global_enable` copies their block
# in below.
